{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"N64\",\"lines\":\"-r--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N64.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"ءَاتُونِىٓ\",\"target_ar\":\"نَارًا\",\"after\":\"The camel in heat stands beside fire used to brand an animal. Together they make an image of a heated body receiving a mark.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ءَاتُونِىٓ names a she-camel in estrus (ضبعت وأرادت الفحل); نارًا also means fire used for branding animals (السمة بها).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N65\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N66\",\"lines\":\"n-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N66.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"أُفْرِغْ\",\"target_ar\":\"ءَاتُونِى\",\"after\":\"An empty condition can be answered by bringing material to fill it.\",\"reason\":\"الخلو بعد الشغل names being empty after work, while ءَاتُونِى means to give or bring (الإيتاء والإعطاء); supply can answer emptiness, though the link is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N66.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"أُفْرِغْ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱنفُخُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The rare sense leaves something empty, while the command to blow sends air into it. The pair makes the heating process sound like emptiness giving way to fullness.\",\"reason\":\"أُفْرِغْ can carry الخلو بعد الشغل, emptiness after work; ٱنفُخُوا۟ means إرسال الريح في الشيء, sending wind into something and filling it.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N67\",\"lines\":\"nn-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N67.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"أُفْرِغْ\",\"target_ar\":\"سَاوَىٰ\",\"after\":\"A broad path made level is one possible image of the work between the cliffs.\",\"reason\":\"فريغ can mean a wide road (طريق فريغ واسع), while سَاوَىٰ means equalizing two things (مساواة ومعادلة); breadth and leveling are compatible features of a passage.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N67.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"أُفْرِغْ\",\"target_ar\":\"بَيْنَ\",\"after\":\"A broad track can run through the space between the two sides.\",\"reason\":\"The rare فريغ sense includes a wide path or broad trace (طريق فريغ واسع); بَيْنَ names the interval between two things (الوسط بين شيئين).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N68\",\"lines\":\"--r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N68.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"أُفْرِغْ\",\"target_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"after\":\"The copper is poured over the barrier, beside the rare image of blood poured out and left unavenged. The metal flow gives that image a new material form.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of أُفْرِغْ says blood is poured out in vain (دمه فرغا، مصبوبا); قِطْرًا is molten copper (النحاس المذاب), which is poured in the verse.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N69\",\"lines\":\"---n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N69.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"أُفْرِغْ\",\"target_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"after\":\"Both senses name fluids, though they belong to very different domains.\",\"reason\":\"The rare أُفْرِغْ sense is male fluid or semen (ماء الرجل، النطفة); قِطْرًا is molten copper (النحاس المذاب).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N70\",\"lines\":\"rr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N70.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"بَيْنَ\",\"after\":\"The side-sense of قِطْرًا meets the between-space named by بَيْنَ. Together they make the gap a bounded place for the metal to fill.\",\"reason\":\"قِطْرًا can mean the sides or flanks (النواحي والجوانب); بَيْنَ means the interval between things (الوسط بين شيئين).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N70.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلصَّدَفَيْنِ\",\"after\":\"The rare side-sense of قِطْرًا echoes the two mountain flanks. The pair makes the worksite read through its opposing sides.\",\"reason\":\"قِطْرًا can mean a side or flank (الجانب); ٱلصَّدَفَيْنِ names the two sides of a mountain pass (جانبا الجبل).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N71\",\"lines\":\"n---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N71.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلصَّدَفَيْنِ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of tipping something onto a side echoes the mountain sides framing the pass.\",\"reason\":\"قِطْرًا can describe throwing someone onto one of their sides (ألقاه على أحد قطريه); ٱلصَّدَفَيْنِ names the two mountain sides (جانبا الجبل).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N72\",\"lines\":\"--r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N72.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"أُفْرِغْ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of قِطْرًا pictures the pour as a succession of drops. The molten sealant reaches the barrier drop by drop as it empties out.\",\"reason\":\"قِطْرًا can mean dripping or drops of water (قطر الماء، جمع قطرة); أُفْرِغْ means pouring or emptying out (الصب وإخلاء الوعاء), of which drops are the small units.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N73\",\"lines\":\"----\"}\n{\"id\":\"N74\",\"lines\":\"--r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N74.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"نَارًا\",\"after\":\"Tree pitch beside fire makes an image of a coating heated until it runs. That image shadows the verse’s fire-state followed by a poured sealant.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قِطْرًا sense is pitch that exudes from a tree and is used as a coating (القطران ما يتحلب من شجر الأبهل، طليته بالقطران); نَارًا is fire (النار المتقدة), which heats or burns pitch.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N75\",\"lines\":\"-rr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N75.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱنفُخُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Blowing beside an incense brazier makes the command evoke kindling its embers. The same breath can feed the fire needed to heat the barrier.\",\"reason\":\"قِطْرًا can mean incense wood and its brazier (عود يتبخر به، المجمرة); ٱنفُخُوا۟ means sending air into something (إرسال الريح في الشيء).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N75.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"نَارًا\",\"after\":\"The incense wood and brazier belong beside the fire that makes them burn. Together they form a picture of fuel, flame, and heat.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قِطْرًا sense names incense wood and its brazier (عود البخور ومجمرته); نَارًا names burning fire (النار المتقدة).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N76\",\"lines\":\"n--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N76.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"بَيْنَ\",\"after\":\"Travel across the land can pass through the space between the two sides.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قِطْرًا sense means going through the land (ذهب في الأرض); بَيْنَ names the interval between two things (الوسط بين شيئين).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N77\",\"lines\":\"nrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N77.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ءَاتُونِى\",\"after\":\"Bringing material can be part of preparing for a fight.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قِطْرًا sense is preparing for combat (التهيؤ للقتال); ءَاتُونِى means bring or supply (الإيتاء والإعطاء), which can provide what that preparation needs.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N77.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ\",\"after\":\"The preparation for combat takes the form of an iron defense. The metal makes readiness visible as a barrier against attack.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قِطْرًا sense is taking position for battle (التهيؤ للقتال); ٱلْحَدِيدِ names iron as a hard, resisting material (الحديد والصلابة الممتنعة).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N77.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"قَالَ\",\"after\":\"The authoritative speaker’s words become a call to prepare for combat. The orders to bring iron and blow make the battle-readiness sense audible in the scene.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قِطْرًا sense means preparing for an attack (تهيأ للحملة); قَالَ introduces speech, and its noun sense can name an authoritative speaker (القيل صاحب القول النافذ).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N78\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N79\",\"lines\":\"r--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N79.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"سَاوَىٰ\",\"after\":\"The rare sale-sense prices the whole lot by comparison with a weighed sample. سَاوَىٰ echoes the equivalence that makes that estimate work.\",\"reason\":\"قِطْرًا can mean selling a bulk lot by weighing a sample and applying that measure to the rest (يأخذ ما بقي على حساب ذلك); سَاوَىٰ means making two things equal (مساواة ومعادلة).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N80\",\"lines\":\"nn-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N80.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ءَاتُونِى\",\"after\":\"A round-trip hire can involve giving or bringing payment.\",\"reason\":\"The rare قِطْرًا sense is hiring for a journey there and back (أكريته ذاهبا وجائيا); ءَاتُونِى means to give or bring (الإيتاء والإعطاء), a possible part of that exchange.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N80.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلصَّدَفَيْنِ\",\"after\":\"The rare round-trip sense supplies a route that could run between the two mountain sides.\",\"reason\":\"قِطْرًا can mean hiring someone to go and return (ذهابا وجيئة); ٱلصَّدَفَيْنِ names the two sides of the pass (جانبا الجبل).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N81\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N82\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N83\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N84\",\"lines\":\"rn-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N84.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of forbidding meets iron’s plain role as a barrier. Together they make the material’s physical blocking echo a prohibition.\",\"reason\":\"زُبَرَ can mean rebuking, restraining, or preventing (الزجر والمنع); ٱلْحَدِيدِ names iron as a boundary or barrier (الحاجز والغاية المميزة).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N84.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱنفُخُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Restraint sits in tension with the command to blow and expand the heated structure.\",\"reason\":\"زُبَرَ can mean restraining or preventing (الزجر والمنع); ٱنفُخُوا۟ means sending wind into something (إرسال الريح في الشيء), an expansive action.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N85\",\"lines\":\"--n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N85.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"target_ar\":\"نَارًا\",\"after\":\"Fire can appear as one form of the rare sense’s calamity.\",\"reason\":\"زُبَرَ can carry the sense of a great calamity (الداهية); نَارًا names burning fire (النار المتقدة), a familiar source of disaster.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N86\",\"lines\":\"--r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N86.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"target_ar\":\"جَعَلَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense gathers the whole material into view as the verse transforms it. The fire-state then seems to take in the full mass, not just a fragment.\",\"reason\":\"زُبَرَ can mean taking something in its entirety (أخذ الشيء كله); جَعَلَهُۥ means rendering the prepared structure into a fire-state (تصيير الشيء على حال).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N87\",\"lines\":\"r--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N87.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱنفُخُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Blowing air into the structure makes the rare image of fibers puffing up vivid. The command can be heard as raising and swelling a surface under pressure.\",\"reason\":\"زُبَرَ can carry the sense of hair or fibers standing up (انتفاش الشعر والوبر); ٱنفُخُوا۟ means sending wind into something (إرسال الريح في الشيء), which can make fibers puff out.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N88\",\"lines\":\"--rn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N88.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"target_ar\":\"أُفْرِغْ\",\"after\":\"The command to pour can evoke a stream of muddy sludge. The rare murk-sense gives the flowing sealant a dense, clouded image.\",\"reason\":\"زُبَرَ can mean mud or murk (الحمأة والكدر); أُفْرِغْ means pouring or emptying out (الصب وإخلاء الوعاء).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N88.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"target_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"after\":\"Muddy sludge and molten copper can share a dense, liquid-like image.\",\"reason\":\"The rare زُبَرَ sense is mud or murk (الحمأة والكدر); قِطْرًا is molten copper (النحاس المذاب).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N89\",\"lines\":\"n-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N89.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ\",\"after\":\"Anger and iron’s toughness meet in a broad image of force.\",\"reason\":\"زُبَرَ can mean anger surging (هاج غضبه); ٱلْحَدِيدِ names hard iron (الحديد والصلابة الممتنعة), so both can suggest strength, though generally.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N89.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱنفُخُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The anger-sense surges, while the command to blow swells the material with air. Together they make the heating phase pulse with expansion.\",\"reason\":\"زُبَرَ can describe anger rising (هاج زبرؤه); ٱنفُخُوا۟ sends wind into something (إرسال الريح في الشيء), making it swell.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N90\",\"lines\":\"r-n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N90.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ\",\"target_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"after\":\"The iron barrier physically blocks passage, echoing the rare sense of prohibition. The two words make the wall’s material and its function reinforce one another.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ can carry the root sense of preventing or blocking (المنع والحظر); زُبَرَ names dense blocks or pieces (قطعة مجتمعة أو كتلة) that can form such a barrier.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N90.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَالَ\",\"after\":\"An authoritative word can prohibit an action, a thin echo of iron’s blocking sense.\",\"reason\":\"The rare حَدِيد sense means preventing or turning something away (المنع والصرف); قَالَ means uttering speech and can introduce an authoritative speaker (القول النافذ).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N91\",\"lines\":\"r--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N91.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلصَّدَفَيْنِ\",\"after\":\"The rare resistance-sense meets two mountain faces set opposite each other. Their opposed sides make the pass feel like a place of confrontation.\",\"reason\":\"The rare حَدِيد sense means resistance or opposition (المحادة والمخالفة); ٱلصَّدَفَيْنِ names the two sides of the pass (جانبا الجبل), which face one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N92\",\"lines\":\"-r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N92.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَالَ\",\"after\":\"The rare sharp-edge sense makes the spoken word seem able to cut. The speaker’s utterance takes on the force of a sharpened blade.\",\"reason\":\"حَدِيد can describe a sharp tongue (ألسنة حداد) or piercing edge (حد السيف); قَالَ names spoken words (إخراج القول بالنطق).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N93\",\"lines\":\"nnr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N93.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ\",\"target_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"after\":\"Iron’s strength and the dense blocks meet in a general image of sturdy material.\",\"reason\":\"The rare حَدِيد sense includes a man’s force or toughness (حد الرجل بأسه); زُبَرَ names a gathered mass or block (قطعة مجتمعة أو كتلة).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N93.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ\",\"target_ar\":\"نَارًا\",\"after\":\"Angry force and fire can meet in the familiar image of heat and fierceness.\",\"reason\":\"The rare حَدِيد sense includes anger and fierce force (الحدة الغضبة، حد الرجل بأسه); نَارًا names burning fire (النار المتقدة).\"}\n{\"id\":\"N93.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ\",\"target_ar\":\"قِطْرًا\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of iron’s toughness stands opposite molten copper’s fluid state. The two materials make the barrier’s hard frame and flowing sealant sharply distinct.\",\"reason\":\"حَدِيد can mean toughness and strength (صلابة الشراب وبأس الرجل); قِطْرًا is molten copper (النحاس المذاب), hard force set against liquid metal.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N94\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N95\",\"lines\":\"r--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N95.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْحَدِيدِ\",\"target_ar\":\"زُبَرَ\",\"after\":\"The iron blocks are the raw material from which iron tools can be made. The rare tool-use sense makes the supplied mass one stage in an object’s working.\",\"reason\":\"The rare حَدِيد sense is using iron for sharpening or shaving (استعمال الحديد); زُبَرَ names collected pieces or blocks (قطعة مجتمعة أو كتلة), possible stock for iron implements.\"}"}}
